QUESTION:- 
Configure your system so that it is an NTP client of utility.domain15.example.com
The system time should be set to your (or nearest to you) timezone and ensure NTP sync is configured

##Step 1: Verify Chrony Installation
rpm -q chrony

#if not installed 
dnf install -y chrony

##Step 2: Set System Timezone
List available timezones:
timedatectl list-timezones | grep -i Asia/Kolkata

Set timezone 
timedatectl set-timezone Asia/Kolkata

Verify 
timedatectl 

##Step 3: Configure NTP Server
vi /etc/chrony.conf
under first line called # These servers were defined in the installation: add

server utility.domain15.example.com iburst
or
server <IP_addr> iburst 
save and exit

##Step 4: Start and enable Chrony Service
systemctl start chronyd
systemctl enable --now chronyd

##Step 5: Force immediate sync
chronyc makestep 

##Step 6: Verify NTP Synchronization 
timedatectl

expected output is:- 
System clock synchronized: yes
NTP service : active

check NTP sources:-
chronyc sources -v
Expected :- ^* utility.domain15.example.com

^* - currently selected NTP server (Sync OK)
^+ - Valid candidate server 
^- -  Valid but not selected 
^? - Unreachable / No response
^x - False time Source 
